<% content_for :title, "Sign in" %>

<h1>Sign in</h1>

<%# Flashes are rendered by the layout.

    data-turbo="false" makes signing in a full page load rather than a Turbo visit. Signing in
    changes who this browser is, and an Action Cable socket keeps the identity it connected
    with: a document that opened a socket as a viewer and then signed in without leaving that
    document would carry the old identity to the next subscription, and MatchStreamAuthorization
    would refuse it that seat's stream (measured: the creator's page missed the join). A full
    load ends the document and the socket with it. The same attribute is on the sign-up form
    and on the sign-out button in the layout, which are the other two ways identity changes. %>
<%= form_with url: session_path, class: "form", data: { turbo: false } do |form| %>
  <div class="form__field">
    <%= form.label :email_address, "Email address" %>
    <%= form.email_field :email_address, required: true, autofocus: true,
          autocomplete: "username", value: params[:email_address] %>
  </div>

  <div class="form__field">
    <%= form.label :password, "Password" %>
    <%= form.password_field :password, required: true, autocomplete: "current-password",
          maxlength: 72 %>
  </div>

  <%= form.submit "Sign in" %>
<% end %>

<p class="form__aside">
  <%= link_to "Forgot your password?", new_password_path %><br>
  No account yet? <%= link_to "Sign up", new_registration_path %>.
</p>
